From a9ce5e97138ace83c62deb8273db618a1586bd9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:24:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(orm): make Preload join aliases deterministic

Preload used bob.NextUniqueInt() for the alias suffix of every joined
table, so building the same query twice produced different SQL. This
defeats statement caches keyed by the SQL text, such as pgx's automatic
prepared statement cache.

Derive the suffix from the join's position in the preload tree (parent
alias, relationship name and side index) instead. The same query now
always builds to the same SQL, while different relationships, or the
same relationship under different parents, still get distinct aliases.
PreloadAs is unchanged.

Closes #741
